  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts with the whole scene. It passes the typecheck, but I couldn't build it or run it in a browser, so none of it has been seen rendering.\n\n- **Island:** a flat-shaded heightfield with jittered vertices and a color for each face (sand, grass, rock, snow cap). Trees are instanced trunks with two cone layers each, and the rocks are rotated boxes.\n- **Water:** a 160-unit wave mesh with a custom shader. Waves are animated in the vertex stage, and the fragment stage adds a fresnel sky reflection, a shallow-water tint near the island and a sun or moon glint. Sky color, light direction and daylight level are updated every frame.\n- **Day/night cycle:** one full cycle takes 20 seconds. The sun and moon lights move along arcs, and sun color goes warm near the horizon. The Preetham sky, with stars, and the fog color follow the sun.\n- **Lighting:** a hemisphere fill light never drops below 0.45 intensity, and the moon light takes over at night, so the scene is never black.\n- **Camera:** it orbits slowly at radius 29 and height 13, aimed at the island so the whole island is in frame.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the first frames are drawn.\n\nThe shader's vec3 uniform writes (`lightDir`, `lightCol`, `skyCol`) are the part most likely to need a fix, since the typecheck doesn't exercise them.\n\n",
